# T line: T2 data/models, fix8 recipe, and --face-camera 0 (docs/DANCE_QUALITY_DEFECTS.md §91, 2026-09-23).
# NOT the default: no operator verdict yet (current.argv keeps t2.argv).
# = t2_fix8.argv with --face-camera 0.7 -> 0.  Strength 0 still applies face_camera's RIGID part (the
#   clip's mean facing put on the lens, "costs exactly nothing" per its docstring); only the SLOW
#   pull-back of sustained turns is dropped.  That pull is what aborted turns ("转身一半"):
#   completed turns (yaw excursion >= 150 deg) test/val GT 12/24, fix8 7/12, this 11/18; aborted share
#   85%/81% -> 75%/75% (GT 74%/69%), per clip 3/14 and 2/21 higher (val P<0.001); off-camera share
#   0.041/0.047 -> 0.116/0.107 against GT 0.123/0.113.  Plan and all 201/294 retrieved units are
#   identical to fix8; joint-angle, turn-back and beat-contrast columns unchanged.
# The face_camera pull was added 2026-09-08 for an arm that was 29.9% off camera with a 1.5 s median
# longest off-camera run; under this recipe the dance without the pull is at ground truth's level.
